"Medium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=820)\nciteturn18view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=820\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 32\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [820].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 820   METHANOTROPH 1A MEDIUM\nL11: NaNO_{3}  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL12: MgSO_{4}·7H_{2}O  | ` 0.1    `  | g\nL13: NaHPO_{4}·12H_{2}O  | ` 0.4    `  | g\nL14: KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 0.22   `  | g\nL15: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.03   `  | g\nL16: FeSO_{4}·7H_{2}O  | ` 2.0    `  | mg\nL17: Trace metal solution (see below)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL18: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL19: Adjust pH to 6.5.\nL20: Distribute the medium into culture vessels (leave >80% volume gas phase), seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave. After cooling, add filter-sterilized methane gas to make a final concentration about 20% (v/v) methane in the gas phase.\nL21: Trace mineral solution:\nL22: ZnSO_{4}·7H_{2}O  | ` 0.44   `  | g\nL23: CuSO_{4}·5H_{2}O  | ` 0.20   `  | g\nL24: MnSO_{4}·xH_{2}O  | ` 0.17   `  | g\nL25: Na_{2}MoO_{4}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.06   `  | g\nL26: H_{3}BO_{3}  | ` 0.10   `  | g\nL27: CoCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 0.08   `  | g\nL28: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL29: * * *\nL30: \nL31: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn18view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=643\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=643 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=650)\nciteturn18view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=650\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 29\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [650].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 650   THIOPHAEOCOCCUS MEDIUM\nL11: KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 0.5    `  | g\nL12: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.15   `  | g\nL13: MgSO_{4}7H_{2}O  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL14: NH_{4}Cl  | ` 0.64   `  | g\nL15: NaCl  | ` 20.0    `  | g\nL16: Yeast extract  | ` 0.4    `  | g\nL17: Sodium pyruvate  | ` 3.0    `  | g\nL18: Trace element solution SL8 (see Medium No. 【0†190】)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL19: NaHCO_{3} (10%, w/v)  | ` 10.0    `  | ml\nL20: Vitamin B_{1}_{2} (2 mg/ml)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL21: Na_{2}S·9H_{2}O (final conc.)  | ` 1.0    `  | mM\nL22: Na_{2}S_{2}O_{3}·5H_{2}O (final conc.)  | ` 6.0    `  | mM\nL23: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL24: Adjust pH to 7.5.\nL25: After autoclaving, add filter-sterilized vitamin B_{1}_{2}, NaHCO_{3}, Na_{2}S·9H_{2}O and Na_{2}S_{2}O_{3}·5H_{2}O solutions to the medium.\nL26: * * *\nL27: \nL28: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn18view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=908\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=908 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=713)\nciteturn18view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=713\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 71\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [713].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 713   THERMOVORAX SUBTERRANEUS MEDIUM\nL11: Solution A:\nL12: KH_{2}PO_{4} ` 0.42   ` g\nL13: Na_{2}HPO_{4} ` 0.43   ` g\nL14: Glucose ` 5.0    ` g\nL15: Resazurin ` 1.0    ` mg\nL16: Distilled water ` 800.0    ` ml\nL17: Mix components thoroughly. Distribute into culture vessels under a N_{2} gas atmosphere (e.g., 45 ml in 100 ml serum bottle), seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.\nL18: Solution B:\nL19: NH_{4}Cl ` 0.3    ` g\nL20: NaCl ` 0.3    ` g\nL21: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O ` 0.11   ` g\nL22: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O ` 0.1    ` g\nL23: Trace mineral solution (see below) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL24: Vitamin solution (see below) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL25: Se-W solution (see below) ` 1.0    ` ml\nL26: Distilled water ` 47.0    ` ml\nL27: Mix components thoroughly. Filter-sterilize and store under a N_{2} gas atmosphere.\nL28: Solution C:\nL29: L-Cysteine·HCl·H_{2}O ` 0.5    ` g\nL30: Yeast extract (BD-Difco) ` 0.2    ` g\nL31: NaHCO_{3} ` 0.4    ` g\nL32: Distilled water ` 49.0    ` ml\nL33: Mix components thoroughly. Filter-sterilize and store under a N_{2} gas atmosphere. Then add the following solution (filter-sterilized) aseptically and anaerobically:\nL34: 24% Na_{2}S·9H_{2}O ` 1.0    ` ml\nL35: To complete medium, add 2.5 ml Solution B and 2.5 ml Solution C to the culture vessels containing 45.0 ml of the medium (Solution A).\nL36: Trace mineral solution:\nL37: 25% HCl (7.7 M) ` 10.0    ` ml\nL38: FeCl_{2}·4H_{2}O ` 2.0    ` g\nL39: H_{3}BO_{3} ` 0.05   ` g\nL40: ZnCl_{2} ` 0.05   ` g\nL41: CuCl_{2}·2H_{2}O ` 0.04   ` g\nL42: MnCl_{2}·4H_{2}O ` 0.04   ` g\nL43: (NH_{4})_{6}Mo7O_{7}·4H_{2}O ` 0.05   ` g\nL44: AlCl_{3} ` 0.05   ` g\nL45: CoCl_{2}·6H_{2}O ` 0.05   ` g\nL46: NiCl_{2}·6H_{2}O ` 0.08   ` g\nL47: EDTA ` 0.5    ` g\nL48: Distilled water ` 987.0    ` ml\nL49: Dissolve FeCl_{2}·4H_{2}O in HCl solution at first. Then add 300 ml distilled water and dissolve the remaining components. Fill up to 1.0 L.\nL50: Vitamin solution:\nL51: Biotin ` 2.0    ` mg\nL52: Folic acid ` 2.0    ` mg\nL53: Pyridoxine·HCl ` 10.0    ` mg\nL54: Thiamine·HCl ` 5.0    ` mg\nL55: Riboflavin ` 5.0    ` mg\nL56: Nicotinic acid ` 10.0    ` mg\nL57: DL-Calcium pantothenate ` 5.0    ` mg\nL58: Vitamin B_{1}_{2} ` 5.0    ` mg\nL59: p-Aminobenzoic acid ` 5.0    ` mg\nL60: Lipoic acid ` 5.0    ` mg\nL61: Distilled water ` 100.0    ` ml\nL62: Se-W solution:\nL63: 10 mM NaOH solution ` 10.0    ` ml\nL64: Na_{2}WO_{4}·2H_{2}O ` 26.5    ` mg\nL65: Na_{2}SeO_{3}·5H_{2}O ` 33.0    ` mg\nL66: Distilled water ` 990.0    ` ml\nL67: Dissolve Na_{2}WO_{4}·2H_{2}O and Na_{2}SeO_{3}·5H_{2}O in 10 mM NaOH solution at first. Then dilute with distilled water.\nL68: * * *\nL69: \nL70: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=776)\nciteturn18view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=776\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 46\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [776].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 776   MH1 MEDIUM FOR SALIARCHAEUM RUBRODURUM\nL11: L-Glutamic acid  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL12: Trisodium citrate·2H_{2}O  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL13: KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL14: NH_{4}Cl  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL15: K_{2}SO_{4}  | ` 5.0    `  | g\nL16: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 20.0    `  | g\nL17: NaCl  | ` 200.0    `  | g\nL18: Casamino acids (BD-Difco)  | ` 4.0    `  | g\nL19: Yeast extract (BD-Difco)  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL20: 0.2% FeSO_{4}·6H_{2}O solution  | ` 2.0    `  | ml\nL21: Trace metal solution  | ` 2.0    `  | ml\nL22: Add components to distilled water and bring volume to 1.0 L. Adjust pH to 5.0 with KOH.\nL23: For preparation of solid medium, add the components listed above (reduce the amount of NaCl to 150.0 g) to distilled water and bring volume to 800.0 ml. Separately prepare the following solution:\nL24: NaCl  | ` 50.0    `  | g\nL25: Agar  | ` 20.0    `  | g\nL26: Distilled water  | ` 200.0    `  | ml\nL27: Combine both solutions after autoclaving.\nL28: Trace metal solution:\nL29: CoCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 0.3    `  | g\nL30: MnCl_{2}·4H_{2}O  | ` 0.1    `  | g\nL31: ZnCl_{2}  | ` 0.1    `  | g\nL32: H_{3}BO_{4}  | ` 0.02   `  | g\nL33: Na_{2}MoO_{4}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.10   `  | g\nL34: NiCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 0.10   `  | g\nL35: CuCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.01   `  | g\nL36: AlCl_{3}  | ` 0.04   `  | g\nL37: Na_{2}WO_{4}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.02   `  | g\nL38: CaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL39: BaCl_{2}·2H_{2}O  | ` 0.1    `  | g\nL40: Na_{2}S_{2}O_{3}·5H_{2}O  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL41: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL42: Adjust pH to 4.0 with HCl.\nL43: * * *\nL44: \nL45: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=461)\nciteturn18view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=461\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 24\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [461].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 461   CHOPPED MEAT MEDIUM\nL11: Ground beef (fat free)  | ` 500.0    `  | g\nL12: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL13: 1 N NaOH  | ` 25.0    `  | ml\nL14: Use lean beef or horse meat. Remove fat and connective tissue before grinding. Mix meat, water and NaOH, then boil for 15 min with stirring. Cool to room temperature, skim fat off surface and filter, retaining both meat particles and filtrate. Add water to the filtrate to a final volume of 1.0 L and then add the following:\nL15: Casitone (BD-Difco)  | ` 30.0    `  | g\nL16: Yeast extract (BD-Difco)  | ` 5.0    `  | g\nL17: K_{2}HPO_{4}  | ` 5.0    `  | g\nL18: Resazurin  | ` 1.0    `  | mg\nL19: Boil, cool, add 0.5 g L-cysteine·HCl·H_{2}O and adjust pH to 7.0. Dispense 7 ml into tubes containing meat particles (use 1 part meat particles to 4 or 5 parts fluid) under a N_{2} atmosphere and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Autoclave at 121C for 30 min. For agar slants, use 15 g agar per 1.0 L medium. Alternatively, commercially available Cooked Meat Medium may be used (Oxoid CM81; Merck 10928; Difco 0267-01-7).\nL20: The medium should be supplemented with 5 g/L yeast extract, 5 g/L K_{2}HPO_{4}, 1 mg/L resazurin, and 0.5 g/L L-cysteine·HCl·H_{2}O.\nL21: * * *\nL22: \nL23: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1385)\nciteturn18view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1385\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 17\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [1385].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 1385   YCFA MEDIUM WITH MANNITOL\nL11: \nL12: Use Medium No. 【0†1130】 with 0.2% mannitol.\nL13: \nL14: * * *\nL15: \nL16: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n"
